<%# Answer-style selects: how the answers are written.
    One control per dimension, showing the stored step and offering the other
    two -- the six pills this replaced spelled out every step permanently and
    filled the whole line under a 380px panel.

    Auto-submit on change, the established pattern for a select that IS a
    setting (scope chip, meetings overview, time session groups). The response
    is a turbo_stream, which Turbo applies wherever it lands, so this form
    deliberately carries NO turbo_frame: it does not navigate anything. %>
<%# In the panel's settings since 2026-11-19 (D9 of the writing-zone plan), beside
    the persona: a standing choice per person, not something set per message, and
    the writing zone had five rows. Laid out like the persona control above it: a
    label, then the full-width select. The DOM class stays the turbo_stream
    replace target. %>
<div class="<%= dom_class %> mt-5 flex flex-col gap-4">
  <% dimensions.each do |dimension| %>
    <div>
      <span class="block text-xs font-bold text-cream-900" aria-hidden="true"><%= group_label(dimension) %></span>
      <%# aria-label rather than a <label for>: the name is the visible word above,
          and a generated field id is what the DOM class above is careful to avoid. %>
      <%= form_with url: update_path(dimension), method: :patch,
                    data: { controller: 'auto-submit' }, class: 'mt-2 block' do |form| %>
        <%= form.select :level,
                        options_for_select(level_options(dimension), selected_level(dimension)),
                        {},
                        name: 'level', id: nil,
                        class: select_classes(dimension),
                        aria: { label: group_label(dimension) } %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-xs text-muted"><%= t('views.organisations.assistant_panels.settings.style_hint') %></p>
</div>
